= Scope

This Supporting Information describes how the data shown in the main-text figures were collected and processed.

Analysis source and cached intermediate data are available at #link("https://github.com/janosh/pymatgen-2-paper"). GitHub, OpenAlex, and the pymatgen repository continue to change; the archived data associated with the article define the snapshot used for the figures.

= S1. OpenAlex citation topics (main-text Fig. 1)

The original pymatgen article was identified by OpenAlex work ID `W2015197254`. Works citing this article were queried through the OpenAlex Works API and grouped by their OpenAlex primary topic. Up to 50 topic groups were retrieved, and groups containing fewer than 10 citing works were excluded. The OpenAlex data were retrieved around 5 July 2025. OpenAlex primary topics are algorithmically assigned; the subsequent language-model grouping therefore formed a second classification layer.

The retained topic names and OpenAlex counts were supplied to OpenAI's GPT-5 model (`gpt-5`), which was prompted to organize them into five thematic branches with concise labels. The branches were ordered by their summed subtopic counts, and the four highest-count subtopics in each branch were retained. The labels and counts returned by the model were cached as structured data; these cached values are preserved in the revised figure. The 20 displayed subtopics sum to 2,699 citing-work assignments. This is a selected thematic summary rather than an exhaustive partition of citations. Branch counts sum the displayed children, and node colors and legend ticks share a logarithmic Viridis scale from 1 to the largest branch count, 1,253.

= S2. Shells of influence (main-text Fig. 2)

The repository-level values were collected from the #link("https://github.com/materialsproject/pymatgen")[`materialsproject/pymatgen`] GitHub repository in August 2026. The contributor total of 276 counts distinct authors of non-bot PRs merged through 31 December 2025, the same population as main-text Fig. 6. The GitHub dependency graph supplied counts of 2,713 dependent repositories and 626 dependent packages. These values refer to the original pymatgen repository and package rather than `pymatgen-core`.

Merged PRs were retrieved through the GitHub REST API and counted by calendar year of merge, rather than creation year. Bot-authored PRs were identified by GitHub usernames ending in `[bot]`, matched case-insensitively. Annual counts with and without bot-authored PRs are listed below.

