The first recorded PR merge occurred on 29 April 2013; 2013 is marked as an incomplete year of PR activity and excluded from the annual average. Over the 12 calendar years from 2014 through 2025, 2,454 non-bot PRs were merged, giving an average of 204.5 merged PRs per year.

PyPI download counts were obtained from the public PyPI download data in Google BigQuery. Counts from August 2018 through December 2025 summed to 23,239,954 and were displayed as approximately 23.2 million. August 2018 was used as the starting month because the PyPI download pipeline significantly under-reported totals before 26 July 2018, as described in the #link("https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/analyzing-pypi-package-downloads/#caveats")[Python Packaging User Guide].

The Materials Project values came from a #link("https://newscenter.lbl.gov/2026/01/13/accelerating-discovery-how-the-materials-project-is-helping-to-usher-in-the-ai-revolution-for-materials-science/")[Berkeley Lab article published on 13 January 2026], which reported approximately 5,000 uses per day and more than 650,000 registered users. The daily use rate was converted to approximately 1.8 million uses per year.

= S3. Upstream and downstream package usage (main-text Fig. 3)

Both panels were derived by statically analyzing Python files and code cells in Jupyter notebooks. Calls to APIs imported from the package were counted and resolved through their import aliases. Dynamically constructed calls were not counted. Link widths represent the resulting function call counts.

== S3.1 APIs of dependencies used by pymatgen (Fig. 3a)

Required dependencies were read from pymatgen's `pyproject.toml` file. Source code at pymatgen commit `ab34799d8ab5dee80756489cf2ca28a97de78121` was analyzed. Calls to each dependency were counted in the `alchemy`, `analysis`, `core`, `electronic_structure`, `entries`, `io`, `phonon`, `symmetry`, and `transformations` subpackages. Dependencies and subpackages with fewer than 15 total calls were omitted from the figure.

== S3.2 pymatgen APIs used by downstream repositories (Fig. 3b)

